  "content_en": "The concubine seeks to marry the best princess. \"Mother, eldest aunt, Xiaojiu suddenly remembered that I haven't finished the homework assigned by Master Yun today, so Xiaojiu is going back first.\" After explaining the technique of the candle, Sister Wenjiu felt that it was time to retreat, so she used the class as an excuse. The girls from the Ninh Binh Hou Mansion would go to a small courtyard near the garden to study with an old master after paying their respects every morning. It is said to be learning, but in fact it is just reading words and tracing red lines, and then adding books such as \"Female Commandments\", \"Internal Training\", \"The Analects of Confucius\" and \"Nv Fan Jie Lu\", which is very boring and single. Even so, this still makes many others admire him, including Jiang and Yan, because both of them were born in merchants and were illiterate. Undoubtedly, this was indeed a good excuse. When Mrs. Jiang heard this, she immediately nodded and smiled, \"Oh, that's it, then I won't keep you. You can't be careless in studying!\" Sister Ninth stood up, and Mrs. Jiang motioned to Mother Zhou to send her off. But at this moment, Mrs. Yan suddenly stood up, took her hand, and took off a jasper bracelet from her wrist to give it to her. Of course Sister Wenjiu had to shirk it. This bracelet was moist and translucent, and it was worth a lot at first glance. It was also Yan's personal belongings, so how could she dare to accept it? Seeing that she refused, Mrs. Yan didn't insist. She just clapped her hand and praised her with a smile, \"What a good child!\" \"Okay, stop looking, weren't you still laughing at me in your heart when I let her in just now.\" Mrs. Jiang looked at Yan, who was staring straight at Sister Wenjiu's back, and teased with a smile. \"Ha... this child is indeed a good one. How come I didn't notice it before!\" Mrs. Yan was not embarrassed by her sister-in-law's words. She looked away and said with a smile. After hearing Yan's words, the corners of Jiang's lips immediately turned up, \"It's only been two years since I moved to the main courtyard. Not only have I become more dignified and generous, but I'm also much more transparent than before. It's a peace of mind.\" Her tone was full of pride. \"This is the credit of my sister's teaching, otherwise my aunt would not be so decent.\" Yan naturally complimented her in a timely manner. \"Where is it...\" Mrs. Jiang smiled proudly, but her face darkened in an instant, \"I didn't teach Sister Ten, but she has the mentality of a child all day long.\" \"It would be better if she was older!\" Mrs. Yan comforted her, and then said suddenly. He suddenly asked, \"This Ninth Sister will be thirteen after the Chinese New Year, right?\" \"Sister-in-law, why are you asking this?\" These words made Jiang's face instantly change, and she became alert, \"You can't be... But weren't you still talking about the Fifth Sister a few days ago? \"Yes, compared to your third master, I hope Brother Xing can find a father-in-law who can stand up to him, but those two girls are both a bit too temperamental. The fifth sister is arrogant and the eighth sister is cowardly. Neither of them can compare with this.\" Girl...\" The fifth sister is the concubine of the second master Wen Chonghe, but she is a noble and arrogant person. When facing the second wife Miao, who is also aloof and arrogant, she will occasionally cause some disharmony in the prince's mansion and provide people with something to talk about after dinner. The eighth sister Wen was the concubine of the eldest master Wen Chongjiang. Her mother died early and she was raised in the eldest wife Zou's courtyard. However, she was weak, dull and timid. \"Sister-in-law, what did you say?\" Before she could finish her words, Ms. Jiang's face turned cold and she turned to look out the window cautiously. She didn't see Zhou's mother in a lake-blue jacket and then said, \"Although she is a concubine, do you think you can choose this girl from the Ningping Hou Mansion? If the old lady hears this, she will be very angry. No matter how rich the Jiang family is, they are still merchants, and no matter how empty the Hou Mansion is, they are also famous for their aristocratic family. \"Sister, what are you doing?\" Yan said in a sarcastic tone, \"Isn't this just gossip between the two of us? Things have been going on for a long time, but the old lady is still thinking about holding her great-grandson in her arms. Hey, sister, you don’t know how difficult it is and how anxious I am...\" As she spoke, Yan's eyes became red again and she took out the handkerchief to wipe her tears. \"Okay, okay, sister-in-law, stop being like this... I went too far, don't worry, I will keep Brother Xing's matter in mind.\" Seeing this scene, Mrs. Jiang instantly softened her heart and quickly pulled Ms. Yan to apologize. \"Hey, I don't blame my sister, it's my sister-in-law who went overboard.\" Mrs. Yan also said that the two of them chatted for a while, and Mrs. Yan didn't stay any longer, stood up and said goodbye to Mrs. Jiang. \"Didn't you agree to have dinner?\" Mr. Jiang left her alone. \"I won't eat anymore. I have to go back quickly. With this, your eldest brother's heart problem may be cured soon.\" Mrs. Yan waved to Mr. JiangHe shook the half of the colorful candle that Sister Jiu left behind just now and said with a smile. Seeing the things in Yan's hands, Jiang couldn't help but smile... At dusk, in the three small houses with three rooms facing each other in the Wen Mansion - \"... what do you think we are... After a long time of fussing, the candles we made are gone, the girl didn't take the bracelet given by the uncle's wife, and the box dowry for the third girl is still missing. After all, it's not like nothing has been done...\" \"Isn't it right, Qingtao, at least my sister-in-law. \"Mother pleases the third lady...\" \"Happiness is nothing, I can't eat it!\" \"Okay, okay, the girl must have a reason for doing this...\" Sister Wenjiu sat by the window and took advantage of the light outside to read a book about people's livelihood and farming for a while. Her eyes were sore after reading it, and she stood up and prepared to do some activities. However, as soon as she walked around the iron flower and bird screen, the conversation between the two little girls could be heard. Sister Wenjiu couldn't help but smile, and instead of walking out, she turned back, walked to the candlestick on the high table beside the bed, and lit the candle on it. A bright halo instantly filled the room, and Sister Wenjiu stood in front of the candlestick and stared at the burning candle wick in a daze. \"Is Miss Ninth here?\" At this moment, someone outside the door said respectfully. \"Oh, it's Mother Zhao, come in quickly!\" Qingtao greeted the mother-in-law's voice outside. \"No, this old slave is here to deliver food to Miss Ninth. Come on -\" \"Why is mom here in person... Hey, this, this... Is mom correct? This meal...\" Qing Xing's voice was surprised. \"Haha, two eldest sisters, please take it quickly. This crystal elbow was made by the third lady in the kitchen to entertain guests. But when the guests left, the third lady asked the old slave to bring it to Miss Ninth for a toothpaste.\" \"Oh...\" \"Old slave, I won't wait anymore, I want more. Go somewhere else.\" \"Girl, girl...\" Qing Tao hurried in, \"Go and check out today's dinner...\" \"Hey, Qing Tao, the elbow is nothing, I can only eat it!\" But before she could finish, Sister Wen Jiu waved her hand. Qing Tao was startled, then her face turned red. \"Haha...\" Sister Wenjiu laughed, \"Don't worry, everything will be fine. The most important thing is to be patient and have a long-term vision.\" Qingtao was startled again and lowered his head shyly. As expected, Sister Wenjiu was right. After dinner, the third lady sent Cuiqiao over and brought her some money, saying that she wanted her to buy some jewelry on her own, but she understood that the actual purpose was to solve her urgent need. This can be regarded as reciprocating a favor...-------off topic----Dear friends, remember to collect it!",
